.TITLE "cp"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Copies files and directories on macOS. This command creates duplicates of files or
directories from a source to a destination. It is a fundamental utility for
__filesystem management__ and has options for preserving attributes,
recursive copying, and handling symbolic links.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**copy**

.DIV "TLDR"
**cp __source_file__ __destination_file__**
Copies a __source_file__ to a __destination_file__.
> __source_file__: The path to the file to copy. | __destination_file__: The path for the new copied file.

**cp -R __source_directory__ __destination_directory__**
Recursively copies a __source_directory__ and its contents to a __destination_directory__.
> __-R__: recursive flag | __source_directory__: The path to the directory to copy. | __destination_directory__: The path for the new copied directory.

**cp -v __source_file__ __destination_directory__**
Copies a __source_file__ to a __destination_directory__, showing verbose output.
> __-v__: verbose flag | __source_file__: The path to the file to copy. | __destination_directory__: The path to the destination directory.

**cp -p __source_file__ __destination_file__**
Copies a __source_file__ to a __destination_file__, preserving attributes (modes, ownership, timestamps).
> __-p__: preserve attributes flag | __source_file__: The path to the file to copy. | __destination_file__: The path for the new copied file.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`cp` is a core command for managing files. When copying directories, always use the
`-R` (recursive) option. Be cautious when specifying destinations to avoid overwriting
files unexpectedly. Use `cp -i` for interactive prompts before overwriting.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:mv** **mac:rm**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/cp.html
